  "reply": "No, not at the current pace. The month ends in two days, and SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards still has 9 of its 14 items open.\n\nThis thread's workstream is empty, so I searched outside it to find the epic. Everything below is read-only.\n\n**Where it stands** (see the bars below): 5 items are done, 4 are in progress and 5 haven't started. 3 of the 5 done items were finished this month.\n\n**Pace:** Oriel's caption on the chart below says: *\"Least-squares line over 7 whole weeks, R² 0.94, 0.8 a week. At that rate the 9 left get there around Jan 14 (Dec 21 – Mar 16, 80%), if no more are added.\"* So even the early end of that range is late December.\n\n**Things worth a look:**\n- Four items haven't moved in about two months and haven't been started: SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout, SYN-57 Checkout analytics: drop-off by step, SYN-88 Refund to the original payment method when a sailing is cancelled and SYN-98 Apply promo codes at checkout. SYN-99 Save a card for next time is in the same state.\n- SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for about three weeks.\n- SYN-23 Pay with a phone wallet on the website, SYN-99 Save a card for next time and SYN-104 Handle 3-D Secure challenges in the native checkout have no estimate, so the remaining work could be larger than the item count suggests.\n- Amara Okafor has three of the open items.\n\nIf it helps, I can make a workstream from this epic and its items, so you can follow it in Oriel and propose changes to it."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
